    {
      "id": "a191tk2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Composition of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The atmosphere consists of five main layers: Troposphere, Stratosphere, Mesosphere, Thermosphere, and Exosphere.",
        "Troposphere is the innermost layer containing nearly all weather phenomena and atmospheric water vapor.",
        "Stratosphere contains the ozone layer which absorbs harmful ultraviolet solar radiation.",
        "Mesosphere is the coldest layer of the atmosphere where most meteorites burn up.",
        "Thermosphere contains the Ionosphere, which reflects radio waves back to Earth for telecommunication."
      ],
      "id": "0az3512"
    },
